WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.042
Transport protocols deliver data between application endpoints.

00:00:03.042 --> 00:00:08.258
TCP presents a reliable ordered byte stream with flow and congestion control.

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:12.604
UDP provides datagrams without those guarantees at the UDP layer.

00:00:12.604 --> 00:00:17.385
Applications may add reliability or other features above UDP when needed.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:24.180
For real-time conversation, delayed audio may be less useful than continuing with the current audio.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:32.680
This does not mean all UDP traffic is automatically fast or all real-time protocols ignore loss; the application’s design determines the trade-off.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.066
Which property does TCP provide to applications?

00:00:37.066 --> 00:00:43.355
TCP provides a reliable ordered byte-stream abstraction, not zero delay or unlimited capacity.
